{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115686",
      "title": "Component Cleanup with DestroyRef",
      "lectureOrder": 127,
      "videoOrder": 121,
      "sourceHash": "fb927c69faad9da6eb7653a7f8fc751d84146da8036898106106f9625953315b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 4.44,
          "en": "So ngOnDestroy can be helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.44,
          "end": 7.98,
          "en": "Angular actually also has an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.98,
          "end": 10.35,
          "en": "to this ngOnDestroy method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.35,
          "end": 12.39,
          "en": "a more modern alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.39,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "which won't work in older Angular versions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 18.42,
          "en": "So if you are getting problems with the alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.42,
          "end": 19.8,
          "en": "I'm about to show you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.8,
          "end": 22.293,
          "en": "you should simply use ngOnDestroy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.13,
          "end": 26.07,
          "en": "But here I'll comment out ngOnDestroy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.07,
          "end": 28.909,
          "en": "and I'll get rid of that OnDestroy interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.909,
          "end": 32.223,
          "en": "so that I'm not forced to add ngOnDestroy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.66,
          "end": 37.95,
          "en": "And I'll get rid of that property, this interval property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.95,
          "end": 40.32,
          "en": "because now I'll use a different approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 42.6,
          "en": "for cleaning up this interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.6,
          "end": 44.67,
          "en": "Angular allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.67,
          "end": 49.02,
          "en": "to inject a special value into your Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.02,
          "end": 53.842,
          "en": "A so called DestroyRef, a Destroy reference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.842,
          "end": 56.76,
          "en": "and you can inject it with help of the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.76,
          "end": 59.163,
          "en": "or with help of the inject function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60,
          "end": 63.84,
          "en": "The type you need to inject is DestroyRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.84,
          "end": 67.53,
          "en": "which is imported from @Angular core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 68.68,
          "en": "this (indistinct) here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.38,
          "end": 73.59,
          "en": "DestroyRef is a class provided by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.59,
          "end": 76.86,
          "en": "and by injecting it and storing it in a property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.86,
          "end": 80.82,
          "en": "you can set up a listener with help of that property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.82,
          "end": 84.81,
          "en": "and that injected value that will trigger a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.81,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "whenever the Component into which you injected DestroyRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 91.92,
          "en": "is about to be destroyed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.92,
          "end": 95.78999999999999,
          "en": "And that's that alternative to ngOnDestroy I mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.78999999999999,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "So here for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 100.95,
          "en": "we could now simply store our interval in a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.95,
          "end": 103.852,
          "en": "which is only available in ngOnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.852,
          "end": 107.00999999999999,
          "en": "because right after setting that interval,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.00999999999999,
          "end": 111.03999999999999,
          "en": "we can use DestroyRef to call OnDestroy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.02000000000001,
          "end": 115.17,
          "en": "and register a function that will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.17,
          "end": 119.88,
          "en": "by Angular when this Component is about to be destroyed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.88,
          "end": 122.83,
          "en": "And it's now in here where we could call clearInterval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 126.363,
          "en": "and pass our interval constant to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.429,
          "end": 131.43,
          "en": "That interval constant is only available in ngOnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.43,
          "end": 134.613,
          "en": "but that's also where I'm setting up this Destroy listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 136.77,
          "en": "And you can use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.77,
          "end": 140.79,
          "en": "and set up as many OnDestroy listeners as you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.79,
          "end": 143.19,
          "en": "in any methods of this Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.19,
          "end": 145.14,
          "en": "You cannot just use it once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.14,
          "end": 147.093,
          "en": "You can use it as often as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 152.37,
          "en": "And that's therefore an elegant alternative to ngOnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "which you also should know about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 158.25,
          "en": "It's not available in older Angular versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.25,
          "end": 162.63,
          "en": "but if you are encountering an error related to DestroyRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 165.963,
          "en": "you can simply use ngOnDestroy as an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
